WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:05.390
Richmond, Virginia a success story of the
booming U.S. economy under Trump.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:10.430
Long gone are the days that big tobacco was
synonymous for Richmonds economic prowess.

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:14.970
The economic strength of the states capital
is in banking, finance and bio-technology

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:15.970
now.

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:20.010
But Richmonds success is in stark contrast
to other parts of Virginia

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:24.180
This is Roanoke, south-west of Richmond in
the Blue Ridge Mountains of the Appalachian

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.180
region.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:29.439
The old railroad town and transportation hub
is home for 300 thousand residents.

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:32.800
Meet Dwayne Yancey, editorial page editor
at The Roanoke Times.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.040
He spent decades reporting on the regions
economic woes.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:41.420
The number 1 industry here is healthcare now.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:45.280
The big employer used to be the Railroad,
now its a hospital chain.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:55.929
The further west you go 
the less fortunate the economy will be.

00:00:55.929 --> 00:00:59.699
Welcome to Bristol, Virginia - the birthplace
of Country Music.

00:00:59.699 --> 00:01:00.699
Literally!

00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:04.250
17 thousand residents live on the Virginia
side of town.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:07.950
26 thousand more in the part that is in Tennessee.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:12.890
The state line goes right through town and
the middle of Bristols Stage Street.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:17.210
City manager Randall Eads, just about a year
in the job - is taking us on a city tour in

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:22.320
his golf cart
Bristol has a poverty rate of 23.6 %.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.000
The town just lost another major employer.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.830
A total of 470 people will soon be out of
a job.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:32.049
What was once the local go-to shopping mall
- is no more.

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:36.460
Thats reality in Bristol - despite Trumponomics,
record job growth and tax reform.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:41.350
The Economy is more complex thanjust one party
being in control or one President being in

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:42.510
control.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:49.470
People will say that Mr. Trump is the one
who made the economy boom right now, others

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.999
will say it
was because of President Obama.

00:01:51.999 --> 00:01:55.680
I dont think either one can necessarily take
credit.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:56.680
There is hope.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:00.700
A Chinese company bought American Merchant
and will start textile production in Bristol

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:01.700
soon.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.289
Thats few hundred new jobs, desperately needed.

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:07.060
A local private investor group wants to invest.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.250
They want to build a casino-resort here.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:13.049
That is thinking big and outside the box,
says city manager Randy.

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:17.110
And that is a must for Bristol in this positive
economic climate, because, You know worst

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:22.599
case scenario is, we have a situation where
the national economy takes a dip.

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:26.659
We go into
a recession or depression.

00:02:26.659 --> 00:02:29.340
Bristol will feel the brunt of that at some
point.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.260
And when that happens, when we continue to
loose

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:39.740
business, if people fail to spend, then Bristol
will have a true headache on its hands.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:44.599
Despite the current strong national economy
people here need more investors and businesses

00:02:44.599 --> 00:02:45.459
betting on Bristol.

